# UI and localization rules

- Arabic (`ar`) is default and RTL; English (`en`) is LTR.
- Set document `lang` and `dir`; use logical CSS rather than left/right
  assumptions.
- Add every system-owned string to the local translation system, including
  visible copy, accessible names, validation, empty states, confirmations, CSV,
  print, and native-dialog labels.
- Built-in catalogs use stable translation keys.
- Never translate custom categories, supplier names, recipients, document
  numbers, or notes.
- Format dates, numbers, and IQD with `ar-IQ` or `en-IQ`; stored values remain
  locale-neutral.
- Use semantic fields, visible focus, keyboard access, large targets, and status
  text/icons that do not depend on color alone.
- Preserve the warm sand, dark ink, olive, brick, and amber visual language in
  `.impeccable.md`.
- Prefer full-page document forms and visible summaries over nested modal flows.
- Preserve entered values after recoverable errors and announce async status.
- Test live locale switching, restart persistence, long copy, large amounts,
  dense tables, empty/error/warning states, and narrow supported windows.
